WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
INTRO:
Since the creation of Bitcoin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.760
the world’s richest crypto holder who got&nbsp;
the majority of their wealth from crypto was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.360
always Satoshi Nakamoto. This isn’t really that&nbsp;
surprising given that Satoshi created Bitcoin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.240
and owns a total of 1 million bitcoins&nbsp;
which was equivalent to nearly $70 billion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:21.040
at the peak. Over the past year though, there&nbsp;
have been rumors in the community that Satoshi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.320
may have been displaced by Changpeng Zhao or&nbsp;
CZ. But there was never any confirmation from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:32.240
sources like Forbes and Bloomberg. In fact, as&nbsp;
recently as November 2021, Yahoo reported CZ’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.280
net worth to be just $2 billion which is&nbsp;
a far cry from Satoshi’s tens of billions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.760
But more recently, Bloomberg added CZ to their&nbsp;
billionaire’s list, and he comes in around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.800
$90 to $100 billion mark. And that doesn’t&nbsp;
even include his personal crypto holdings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.080
Just 5 years ago though, CZ’s net worth likely&nbsp;
didn’t even cross the $100 million mark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.840
so here’s how CZ made $100 billion in 5 years and&nbsp;
became the world’s richest crypto billionaire.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.440
EARLY LIFE:&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.320
Taking a look back, CZ was born on September&nbsp;
10th, 1977 in the Jiangsu province of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:12.080
China. Both of his parents were teachers by trade,&nbsp;
but this didn’t last very long after CZ’s birth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.440
You see, CZ’s father worked at a university&nbsp;
and was known for having pro-bourgeois beliefs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.800
Bourgeois simply refers to middle and upper-class&nbsp;
people, so that would mean that CZ’s father had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.760
pro-middle-class beliefs. But, such beliefs&nbsp;
were frowned upon in China, and over time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.320
pressure mounted for CZ’s father to leave&nbsp;
the university. So, shortly after CZ’s birth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:37.520
the family exiled to a rural area. This is where&nbsp;
CZ spent the majority of his early childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.560
but when he was 12 years old, his family decided&nbsp;
to move to Vancouver, Canada. It’s not clear what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.680
his parents did for a living in Canada, but&nbsp;
it definitely wasn’t that lucrative. CZ had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.600
to pick up a number of minimum wage service jobs&nbsp;
throughout his teenage years including working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.080
at a few gas stations and McDonald’s. Moving&nbsp;
into his college years, CZ attended McGill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.200
University in Montreal, Quebec where he majored in&nbsp;
computer science. Considering this training in CS,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.520
I don’t think you’d be surprised to hear that CZ&nbsp;
found an internship as a software developer out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:11.200
college. But, it wasn’t at a tech company, it was&nbsp;
actually at the Tokyo Stock Exchange. CZ worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.680
for a subcontractor of the Tokyo Stock Exchange&nbsp;
who was responsible for developing software for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.960
matching buy and sell orders. After his time in&nbsp;
Tokyo, CZ secured a full-time job at Bloomberg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:26.160
Tradebook in 2001. Here, CZ worked as a developer&nbsp;
for futures trading software which lasted for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:32.000
about 4 years until he left in 2005. While CZ&nbsp;
was technically a software developer, his entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.480
career was based on the financial sector. Many&nbsp;
software engineers would probably find this quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.680
boring and would rather work at an innovative&nbsp;
tech company, but CZ didn’t mind. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.680
he spotted great opportunity within the trading&nbsp;
world and this led him to found his first company.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.440
FUSION SYSTEMS:&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.360
One of the biggest shortfalls of the financial&nbsp;
industry is that they’re usually one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.920
last industries to adopt new technologies.&nbsp;
Take bank transfers for example. Most banks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.960
still use ACH transfers to move around money&nbsp;
despite the technology being created in 1972.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:07.680
Usually, this is because with the financial&nbsp;
industry, large amounts of money are involved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.000
and people are reluctant to trust newer&nbsp;
systems. But, when a technological advantage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.360
is undebatably better, people do usually come&nbsp;
around, and this is what CZ was betting on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:23.040
In 2005, CZ founded Fusion Systems in Shanghai,&nbsp;
China. The company specialized in developing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.600
high-frequency trading systems for stockbrokers&nbsp;
that could replace their old clunky systems.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.560
The company also provided IT consulting services&nbsp;
as well. Fusion Systems never turned into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:37.120
billion company or anything, but it looks like&nbsp;
it was enough to provide CZ with a well-off life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.920
He ran the company up until 2013 when&nbsp;
he heard about something called Bitcoin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.480
CZ’s introduction to bitcoin dates back to a&nbsp;
poker game with his friends in the early 2010s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.160
One of his friends mentioned bitcoin and&nbsp;
described what it was trying to accomplish.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.720
CZ wasn’t instantly sold, but he was intrigued&nbsp;
and it didn’t take him long to go down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:00.080
Bitcoin rabbit hole. He started off by just buying&nbsp;
some bitcoin, and then he sold his house and put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:06.160
it all into Bitcoin. Yes, that escalated fast.&nbsp;
Also, let’s not forget, this was way back in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:13.200
2013/2014 bitcoin bull run. Selling your house and&nbsp;
going all-in on bitcoin is not smart even today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.320
and that’s with significant institutional support&nbsp;
and a market cap of around $1 trillion. Back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.840
2013, Bitcoin’s market cap was just $1 billion for&nbsp;
most of the year, and the overwhelming sentiment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:30.400
was that Bitcoin was a scam that was going to&nbsp;
zero. So, I have no clue how CZ was so confident.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.320
On top of gambling his entire net worth&nbsp;
on Bitcoin, CZ decided to leave Fusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:41.840
Systems and get a job within the cryptocurrency&nbsp;
space. So, CZ was literally all in on Bitcoin.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.360
ALL IN:&nbsp;

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.720
CZ’s first job within the crypto-verse was at&nbsp;
Blockchain.com. Blockchain.com was the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:54.240
provider of cryptocurrency wallets and exchange&nbsp;
services. Between 2012 and 2020, they accounted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:59.920
for 28% of all bitcoin transactions. Over the&nbsp;
past few years, Blockchain.com has lost a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:04.240
of its appeal as many consumers have switched&nbsp;
over to more convenient brokerages like Coinbase,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.600
Gemini, and of course Binance. But back in&nbsp;
the day, Blockchain.com was the go-to place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.400
for Bitcoin, and CZ joined as the third member&nbsp;
of the company’s cryptocurrency wallet team.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.000
CZ helped with the software development for&nbsp;
the wallet for one year before he switched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:24.560
over to OKCoin as CTO. At the time, OKCoin was&nbsp;
a rather new platform being founded in 2013.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:29.760
Unlike Blockchain.com which was mainly designed as&nbsp;
a place to hold crypto, OKCoin was more focused on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:35.040
enabling customers to invest and trade with ease.&nbsp;
Today, OKCoin has grown into being one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:40.560
largest crypto brokerages in the world with over&nbsp;
100,000 investors and traders. So, it wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:46.080
have been a bad bet to stay with OKCoin, but CZ&nbsp;
felt that he could create a much better brokerage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:50.160
He already had a decade worth of experience&nbsp;
developing high-frequency stock trading systems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.920
and now he had a pretty solid understanding of the&nbsp;
blockchain. So, in 2015, CZ decided to combine his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:00.880
knowledge and found Bijie Tech. The company was&nbsp;
based in Shanghai and focused on providing crypto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:06.640
exchange services to local residents. Bijie Tech&nbsp;
chugged along for 2 years until suddenly in 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:12.000
all of Bijie’s platforms and websites went dead.&nbsp;
There was never any explanation as to why Bijie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:17.440
was shut down or if it was intentional. We all&nbsp;
know that China is not a big fan of crypto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:22.480
so maybe the shutdown can be explained by&nbsp;
political pressure. Or maybe, CZ shut down Bijie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.520
on purpose in order to launch a more refined and&nbsp;
stable exchange. We may never find out why Bijie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:33.840
was shut down, but what we do know is that this&nbsp;
was just the beginning of CZ’s crypto journey.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:36.480
BINANCE:&nbsp;

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:40.640
CZ was determined to launch another crypto&nbsp;
brokerage, but he had very little cash left,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:45.040
and he was by no means willing to sell his&nbsp;
bitcoin. So, he went to the public markets for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:50.400
help. In 2017, CZ launched a new cryptocurrency&nbsp;
called Binance Coin which was built on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.840
Ethereum network. The initial coin offering raised&nbsp;
a total of $15 million which he used to launch the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:01.600
Binance exchange in July of 2017. To this day,&nbsp;
CZ claims that he only holds two cryptos which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:06.400
are of course Bitcoin and Binance Coin. He says&nbsp;
that the majority of his personal crypto holdings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.360
is Binance Coin, and he has no plans of changing&nbsp;
this. CZ believes that keeping the majority of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:16.320
his personal wealth in Binance keeps him loyal&nbsp;
and committed to the company long-term. Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:20.800
despite the young nature of Binance, traders&nbsp;
flooded in almost immediately as Binance was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:25.520
specifically designed for high-frequency trading.&nbsp;
Within just 8 months, Binance became the world’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:30.000
largest cryptocurrency exchange in terms of&nbsp;
trading volume. And CZ leveraged this popularity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.000
to launch a blockchain network called&nbsp;
Binance Smart Chain. As the name suggests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.560
this was a new crypto blockchain. But, this chain&nbsp;
was more similar to Ethereum’s blockchain than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.400
it was to Bitcoin’s blockchain given that&nbsp;
it was focused on defi applications. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:46.640
includes applications such as smart contracts,&nbsp;
cross-chain transfers, and reduced block times.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:51.680
Aside from launching a cryptocurrency, CZ also&nbsp;
launched a stable coin in 2018. The goal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.680
the stable coin was to allow people to enjoy&nbsp;
the benefits of cryptocurrency and blockchain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.680 --> 00:08:00.720
technology without all the volatility. CZ started&nbsp;
off by partnering with 3 other exchanges and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:05.760
raising a total of $32 million which they used&nbsp;
to launch BUSD which is apparently backed 1 to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:10.880
1 with US dollars. Moving into 2019, Binance&nbsp;
partnered with an Israeli payment processor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.520
called Simplex which allowed for cryptocurrency&nbsp;
purchases to be made with debit and credit cards.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:19.680
Despite all these great expansion efforts&nbsp;
though, it wasn’t all smooth sailing for Binance.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.360
ROUGH WATERS:&nbsp;

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:27.440
From the very beginning, one of the biggest&nbsp;
challenges Binance faced was regulatory issues.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.200
In September of 2017, China announced that&nbsp;
they were going to ban cryptocurrency trading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:35.840
within the country. So, CZ had to move&nbsp;
all of Binance’s operations to Japan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:40.240
This worked for a couple of months, but it didn’t&nbsp;
take long for Japan to start cracking down on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.280
cryptocurrency trading as well. So, in March&nbsp;
of 2018, Binance expanded their operations to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:50.320
the island of Malta and they formed a Memorandum&nbsp;
of Understanding with the Government of Bermuda.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:54.160
This finally allowed them to continue&nbsp;
operations without the fear of being shut down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:57.920
but they were still missing out on the largest&nbsp;
market in the world because the US banned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:03.840
Binance in 2019. As a result, Binance had to&nbsp;
launch a US-specific version called Binance.us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:08.080
which complies with US brokerage rules. This&nbsp;
wasn’t the end of their regulation nightmare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:13.840
either. Even today, Binance is under investigation&nbsp;
by the US for tax evasion and money laundering.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:19.280
But these regulatory issues would pale in&nbsp;
comparison to what would unfold in 2019. On May 7,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:25.440
2019, a group of hackers used phishing and viruses&nbsp;
to steal 7000 bitcoins or $40 million worth of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:31.200
Bitcoins from Binance. Fortunately, this was only&nbsp;
2% of Binance’s total holdings and they were able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:35.840
to cover the losses out of pocket. But, this has&nbsp;
become a permanent black mark on their reputation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:40.960
Aside from having to deal with hackers, Binance&nbsp;
has also had to deal with quite a bit of angry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:46.640
customers. You see, crypto is still a pretty young&nbsp;
technology, and exchanges aren’t always perfect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:51.600
Outages still happen from time to time, and though&nbsp;
Binance likely has a clause that says that they’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:56.400
not responsible for losses caused by outages, some&nbsp;
traders are trying to pursue charges and reclaim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:02.080
losses nonetheless. Honestly, I don’t think this&nbsp;
case will go anywhere, but it’s just another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:08.000
hassle that Binance has to deal with as well.
BINANCE TODAY:&nbsp;

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.560
Despite all these challenges, Binance is still&nbsp;
the largest crypto brokerage in the world in terms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:17.520
of volume. Since they’re a private company, they&nbsp;
don’t release their revenue and earnings number,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:22.320
but we do know that Binance processes up to&nbsp;
$170 billion worth of crypto trades every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:27.520
day. To put that in perspective, Coinbase has a&nbsp;
daily trade volume of just $2 billion per day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.600
Now, of course, Coinbase is not a trading&nbsp;
platform, but given that the majority of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:36.240
these brokerages make their money on transactional&nbsp;
fees, volume is extremely important for profit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:42.160
Even with just $2 billion in volume every day,&nbsp;
Coinbase is valued at $50 billion. So, I don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.960
think you’d be surprised to hear that Binance is&nbsp;
worth well above $100 billion. Looking forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:52.000
CZ aims to donate the vast majority of his wealth&nbsp;
as in 90+% to charity. So, it looks like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:57.360
wealth has found its way to good hands. And that’s&nbsp;
how CZ went from $100 million to $100 billion in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:01.920
5 years. Would you guys have gone all-in on&nbsp;
Bitcoin in 2013? Comment that down below.&nbsp;&nbsp;

